@vinnamkim One thing that is happening in your example is that you are using a "reliable" QoS (that is the default if you don't specify anything).  In that mode, all of the messages must be acknowledged before they are dropped from the queue.  One interesting thing might be to try switching to "Best Effort", and seeing what the results are; in that case, the publisher will forget about the message as soon as it sends it.

The other thing is to ping the Fast-RTPS people to see what they have to say about.  @vinnamkim they will most likely ask for a wireshark capture, so can you please do that?

@richiprosima can you take a look at this and see if this is expected behavior or a bug?
